On Mar 14, 10:33 am, cheepi...@hotmail.com wrote:
> I've been toying with the idea of making a middle/late game
> gameplay patch, that falls somewhere between "Gehennom
> is boring", and "next version wishlist."  I've tried to keep
> the ideas limited to things simple enough for me to code; a
> tough standard.[1]
>
> Anyway, here are some of the more specific ideas.
>
> * HP/SP cap
> The cap would be a bit soft. HP/SP max over the cap would drift
> down towards it at a speed proportional to your healing rate. But
> slow enough where someone could enjoy having huge HP for awhile
> if they really wanted to. Race and class big inputs to the cap.

ehh.  Usually by the time you're good enough to be bored by the late
game, you're no longer bothering to get to 300+ hp before Gehennom.
This kind of just makes first ascensions a little tougher without
helping repeat playability.

> * Diminishing returns on negative AC.
> Leaning towards: DR = min(min(rnd(-ac),rnd(-ac)),20).

Similar.

> * Nerfed Reflection
> Instead of each reflection-giving item granting perfect reflection,
> items would have individual probabilities of reflecting attacks, and
> each item gets a chance to reflect any one attack. Rough shot at
> numbers: artifacts (generally) 90%, AoR 95%, SDSM 99%, SoR 99.9%,
> being-a-SD 100%. Breath weapons harder to reflect.

And this just introduces randomness and makes people have to find ways
to accumulate more stuff.  Seems like it'd increase the boredom factor
to me.

> * But wait, Gehennom is still boring
> Here's what I'm thinking about doing to Gehennom:
> - Make the mazes generally more open, with more monsters initially.

Good.  Maybe add in rivers and other distinguishing features.

> - Shorten it from top to bottom.
> - Move all the lairs out to side branches.

I'd rather keep the lairs in-line, make partial-teleport levels
possible (so you can teleport to the non-tower part of the level from
any point in the level), make one-way diggable walls (maybe /digging
only, so umber hulks/dwarves won't help you, and have it so you can
dig _out_ of the tower once you've gotten in but can't skip things
entirely).

> Lair chosen randomly to have Candelabrum. Other lairs have goodies.

Hmm.  I'd have to think about that.  Maybe some unique non-artifact
items (e.g. introduce shimmering DSM in one).

> - Bonuses for demons and demon princes. HP, speed, resistances,
>   Elbereth-immunity.

They're too weak for the most part, yeah.

> * Some small tweaks, like speed boosts for dragons.

Them too, but making them faster could be an advantage for players as
well (the main reason not to ride dragons now is that they're SLOW).



